        <obo:IAO_0000115>A polydisperse, highly branched glucan composed of chains of D-glucopyranose residues in alpha(1-&gt;4) glycosidic linkage, joined together by alpha(1-&gt;6) glycosidic linkages. A small number of alpha(1-&gt;3) glycosidic linkages and some cumulative alpha(1-&gt;6) links also may occur. The branches in glycogen typically contain 8 to 12 glucose residues.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>CHEBI:24379</oboInOwl:hasAlternativeId>
