        <obo:IAO_0000115>A simple form of learning whereby the repeated presence of a stimulus leads to a change in the probability or strength of the response to that stimulus. There is no association of one type of stimulus with another, rather it is a generalized response to the environment.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>unconditional response</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>biological_process</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>GO:0046958</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>nonassociative learning</rdfs:label>
