        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any process that increases the rate, frequency or extent of microtubule nucleation. Microtubule nucleation is the &apos;de novo&apos; formation of a microtubule, in which tubulin heterodimers form metastable oligomeric aggregates, some of which go on to support formation of a complete microtubule. Microtubule nucleation usually occurs from a specific site within a cell.</obo:IAO_0000115>
