    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000088 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000088">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000861"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The arrangement of the principal muscle cell type whose contractile activity generates body motion in the nematode differs from that observed in control animals. In C. elegans they consist of 95 unfused cells in the adult organized into four muscle quadrants. Their sarcomeres are obliquely striated and lie lengthwise along the body wall (Wormatlas).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>body wall muscle displaced</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0000088</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>body muscle displaced</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000088"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>The arrangement of the principal muscle cell type whose contractile activity generates body motion in the nematode differs from that observed in control animals. In C. elegans they consist of 95 unfused cells in the adult organized into four muscle quadrants. Their sarcomeres are obliquely striated and lie lengthwise along the body wall (Wormatlas).</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>WB:WBPerson2021</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>WB:WBPerson557</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


