        <obo:IAO_0000115>Animals exhibit variations in the structure or composition of the amphid sensillum cell that ensheathes the dendrite tips of channel neurons and wing cell dedritic processes, from that observed in control animals. Sheath cells in C.elegans have highly invaginated and vesiculated surfaces, which provide a specialized environment for the dendritic structures.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>amphid sheath cell morphology abnormal</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0000300</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>amphid sheath cell morphology variant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
