        <obo:IAO_0000115>The structure made by the processes of the excretory canal cell is increased in size compared to control. In C. elegans this is an H-shaped structure which extends almost the full length of the body on both sides of the animal, generally in contact with the lateral hypodermis and the pseudocoelom (Wormatlas).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>long excretory canals</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0000440</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>excretory canals long</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
