                </owl:someValuesFrom>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Animals exhibit variations in the structure or organization of the microtubule-based dendritic projections extending from the cell body, compared to that observed in control animals. In C. elegans, cilia are classified as channel cilia or wing cilia depending on their placement within the sensillum. Channel cilia of control animals are cylindrical, extend into the sensillum pore and are exposed to the outside. Wing cilia of control animals vary in shape, are embedded in the sensillum sheath cell and are not typically refractory to dyes indicating exposure to the outside.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>cilia morphology abnormal</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>defective dye filling of cilia</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0000615</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>cilia morphology variant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000615"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Animals exhibit variations in the structure or organization of the microtubule-based dendritic projections extending from the cell body, compared to that observed in control animals. In C. elegans, cilia are classified as channel cilia or wing cilia depending on their placement within the sensillum. Channel cilia of control animals are cylindrical, extend into the sensillum pore and are exposed to the outside. Wing cilia of control animals vary in shape, are embedded in the sensillum sheath cell and are not typically refractory to dyes indicating exposure to the outside.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>WB:WBPaper00000214</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>WB:WBPaper00000932</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>WB:WBPerson712</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


