        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000727"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any variation in the catalysis of a biochemical reaction compared to control. Catalysts are naturally occurring macromolecular substances known as enzymes. Enzymes possess specific binding sites for substrates, and are usually composed wholly or largely of protein (can include an RNA component).</obo:IAO_0000115>
