        <rdfs:comment>The phenotype ontology was restructured such that &quot;Abnormal&quot; is now the root term.  The term &quot;Abnormal&quot; with a &quot;Not&quot; qualifier is a suggested replacement for this term.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>This phenotype was intended to reflect a lack of any phenotypic abnormality in the individuals in question. The C. elegans phenotype ontology no longer has terms specifically used to assert negation of a phenotype.</rdfs:comment>
