    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0001334 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0001334">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0001335"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any variation in the form, structure or composition of the muscles of the adult hermaphrodite reproductive system compared to control. In C. elegans hermaphrodites these muscles include the vulval and uterine muscles, located near the vulva in the midbody, which all derive from the M myoblast (Wormatlas).</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>hermaphrodite sex muscle morphology abnormal</oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0001334</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>hermaphrodite sex muscle morphology variant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0001334"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Any variation in the form, structure or composition of the muscles of the adult hermaphrodite reproductive system compared to control. In C. elegans hermaphrodites these muscles include the vulval and uterine muscles, located near the vulva in the midbody, which all derive from the M myoblast (Wormatlas).</owl:annotatedTarget>
