        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/WBPhenotype_0000900"/>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Any variation in the form or composition of the compartments in the germline of females/hermaphrodites compared to control animals. In C. elegans these compartments contain a nucleus and are connected to a common cytoplasm (rachis).  These compartments eventually undergo cellularization and become oocytes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>C_elegans_phenotype_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
        <oboInOwl:id>WBPhenotype:0001969</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>germ cell compartment morphology variant</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
