        <obo:IAO_0000115>Animals exhibit variations in the extent to which one or more sensory neurons associated with sensilla (typically one or more amphids and/or phasmids) take up dye from the environment, compared to controls. In C. elegans, these neurons are commonly assayed by dye-filling with FITC, DiI or DiO.</obo:IAO_0000115>
