        <obo:IAO_0000115>Animals exhibit an abnormal attachment (or lack thereof) to a substrate, compared to controls. For some parasitic worms, attachment to host tissue surfaces, like endothelium, is a necessary behavior for their life cycle.</obo:IAO_0000115>
