        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Animals exhibit an abnormal attachment (or lack thereof) to a substrate, compared to controls. For some parasitic worms, attachment to host tissue surfaces, like endothelium, is a necessary behavior for their life cycle.</owl:annotatedTarget>
